From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] relax: cast biotite CellList inputs/outputs for biotite 1.7

Upstream-Status: Issue [https://github.com/biotite-dev/hydride/issues/29]

biotite 1.7 reimplemented structure.CellList in Rust, which changed two
things MinimumFinder.__init__ relies on:

- CellList.get_atoms() now returns int64 indices, so assigning the
  result to the `cdef int32[:,:] adj_indices` memoryview raises
  "ValueError: Buffer dtype mismatch, expected 'int32' but got 'long'"
  for every relax_hydrogen() call (hydride issues #29 and #30).
- CellList(..., periodic=True, box=...) only accepts a float32 box; the
  float64 np.identity(3)-style boxes callers pass raise
  "TypeError: 'ndarray' object cannot be cast as 'ndarray'".

Cast the box to float32 and the returned indices to int32 at the call
site. With biotite 1.7.1 (the only biotite on pypi.riseproject.dev) the
unpatched wheel fails 141 of the 1327 tests on any architecture
(reproduced on x86_64); with this patch they all pass. biotite 1.6.0
and older already return int32 and accept a float32 box, so the casts
are no-ops there.

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 src/hydride/relax.pyx | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/hydride/relax.pyx b/src/hydride/relax.pyx
index 3c937bd..6c94593 100644
--- a/src/hydride/relax.pyx
+++ b/src/hydride/relax.pyx
@@ -218,7 +218,8 @@ class MinimumFinder:
             )
         else:
             cell_list = struc.CellList(
-                atoms, cell_size=force_cutoff, periodic=True, box=self._box
+                atoms, cell_size=force_cutoff, periodic=True,
+                box=np.asarray(self._box, dtype=np.float32)
             )
         relevant_mask = (np.asarray(groups) != -1)
         cdef int32[:] relevant_indices = np.where(relevant_mask)[0] \
@@ -226,7 +227,7 @@ class MinimumFinder:
         cdef int32[:,:] adj_indices = cell_list.get_atoms(
             atoms.coord[np.asarray(relevant_indices)],
             radius=force_cutoff
-        )
+        ).astype(np.int32, copy=False)
 
 
         cdef int32[:,:] bond_indices = atoms.bonds.get_all_bonds()[0]
-- 
